       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Jared Whiklo",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I am guessing that Fedora 4 did not follow the specification and it was implemented in Fedora 6 we tried to follow the specification closer (which was also easier, I think). Section 5.4.1.4 says",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "text": "5.4.1.4 Each LDP Direct Container representation ",
            "type": "text"
           },
           {
            "marks": [
             {
              "type": "em"
             }
            ],
            "text": "MUST",
            "type": "text"
           },
           {
            "text": " contain exactly one triple whose subject is the LDPC URI, and whose predicate is either ",
            "type": "text"
           },
           {
            "marks": [
             {
              "type": "code"
             }
            ],
            "text": "ldp:hasMemberRelation",
            "type": "text"
           },
           {
            "text": " or ",
            "type": "text"
           },
           {
            "marks": [
             {
              "type": "code"
             }
            ],
            "text": "ldp:isMemberOfRelation",
            "type": "text"
           },
           {
            "text": ". The object of the triple is constrained by other sections, such as ",
            "type": "text"
           },
           {
            "marks": [
             {
              "type": "strong"
             }
            ],
            "text": "ldp:hasMemberRelation",
            "type": "text"
           },
           {
            "text": " or ",
            "type": "text"
           },
           {
            "marks": [
             {
              "type": "strong"
             }
            ],
            "text": "ldp:isMemberOfRelation",
            "type": "text"
           },
           {
            "text": ", based on the membership triple pattern used by the container.",
            "type": "text"
           }
          ],
          "type": "paragraph"
         }
        ],
        "type": "blockquote"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "We’ll bring this up at the November 3rd, 2022 tech call as hopefully the person that wrote this code can confirm.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
