    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:0b01ad78-89ae-4048-8816-7ae1630efe61",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f7f04c510197b3b5f5763bf9e891b3f8?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FQH-5.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f7f04c510197b3b5f5763bf9e891b3f8?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FQH-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f7f04c510197b3b5f5763bf9e891b3f8?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FQH-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f7f04c510197b3b5f5763bf9e891b3f8?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FQH-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Quinn Hart",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A0b01ad78-89ae-4048-8816-7ae1630efe61",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "So, it appears that all the commenting facility for the  LDP are all moribund, so I don’t expect to a response on my query there.  I’ll make a plea that if this isn’t hard technically, it’d be worth supporting.  The example we gave above is one good use case, but Fedora 6 is making us rethink containment, in ways that would make this maybe more important for indirect containers.  The basic idea for that is that archive groups are such a nice feature, we want to do a better job of dividing our archive into these groups.  As a result, indirect containers are important to link other archival objects which can’t be contained, like collections of archival group items.  ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "attrs": {
         "language": "none"
        },
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "@prefix ldp:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#> .\n@prefix schema: <http://schema.org/> .\n@prefix : <http://example.org/> .\n<>  ldp:membershipResource <.>;\n    ldp:isMemberOfRelation schema:partOf;\n    ldp:XhasMemberRelation schema:hasPart;\n    ldp:insertedContentRelation schema:hasPart;\n    .",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "codeBlock"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Here it’s really important that the collections know the items they ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "type": "code"
           }
          ],
          "text": "havePart",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": " and equally, items know which collections they are ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "type": "code"
           }
          ],
          "text": "partOf",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "And having to do that twice for both directions, kind of kills your bookkeeping on that.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
