     "body": "<p>I am guessing that Fedora 4 did not follow the specification and it was implemented in Fedora 6 we tried to follow the specification closer (which was also easier, I think). Section 5.4.1.4 says</p>\n\n<blockquote><p>5.4.1.4 Each LDP Direct Container representation <em>MUST</em> contain exactly one triple whose subject is the LDPC URI, and whose predicate is either <tt>ldp:hasMemberRelation</tt> or <tt>ldp:isMemberOfRelation</tt>. The object of the triple is constrained by other sections, such as <b>ldp:hasMemberRelation</b> or <b>ldp:isMemberOfRelation</b>, based on the membership triple pattern used by the container.</p></blockquote>\n\n<p>We’ll bring this up at the November 3rd, 2022 tech call as hopefully the person that wrote this code can confirm.</p>",
