    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:0b01ad78-89ae-4048-8816-7ae1630efe61",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f7f04c510197b3b5f5763bf9e891b3f8?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FQH-5.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f7f04c510197b3b5f5763bf9e891b3f8?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FQH-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f7f04c510197b3b5f5763bf9e891b3f8?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FQH-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f7f04c510197b3b5f5763bf9e891b3f8?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FQH-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Quinn Hart",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A0b01ad78-89ae-4048-8816-7ae1630efe61",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>So, it appears that all the commenting facility for the  LDP are all moribund, so I don’t expect to a response on my query there.  I’ll make a plea that if this isn’t hard technically, it’d be worth supporting.  The example we gave above is one good use case, but Fedora 6 is making us rethink containment, in ways that would make this maybe more important for indirect containers.  The basic idea for that is that archive groups are such a nice feature, we want to do a better job of dividing our archive into these groups.  As a result, indirect containers are important to link other archival objects which can’t be contained, like collections of archival group items.  </p>\n\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-none\">@prefix ldp:   &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#&gt; .\n@prefix schema: &lt;http://schema.org/&gt; .\n@prefix : &lt;http://example.org/&gt; .\n&lt;&gt;  ldp:membershipResource &lt;.&gt;;\n    ldp:isMemberOfRelation schema:partOf;\n    ldp:XhasMemberRelation schema:hasPart;\n    ldp:insertedContentRelation schema:hasPart;\n    .</pre>\n</div></div>\n\n<p>Here it’s really important that the collections know the items they <tt>havePart</tt> and equally, items know which collections they are <tt>partOf</tt></p>\n\n<p>And having to do that twice for both directions, kind of kills your bookkeeping on that.</p>",
     "created": "09/Nov/22 5:35 PM",
     "id": "22758",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/13761/comment/22758",
